  "chapter": {
    "number": 55,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(56) For the end, concerning the people that were removed from the",
          {
            "noteId": 103
          },
          "sanctuary, by David for a memorial, when the Philistines caught him in Geth."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Have mercy upon me, O God; for man has trodden me down; all the day long he warring has afflicted me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Mine enemies have trodden me down all the day from the dawning of the day; for there are many warring against me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They shall be afraid, but I will trust in you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "In God I will praise my words; all the day have I hoped in God; I will not fear what flesh shall do to me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "All the day long they have abominated my words; all their devices are against me for evil.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They will dwell near and hide themselves; they will watch my steps, accordingly as I have waited patiently in my soul.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You will on no account save them; you will bring down the people in wrath.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O God, I have declared my life to you; you have set my tears before you, even according to your promise.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Mine enemies shall be turned back, in the day wherein I shall call upon you; behold, I know that you are my God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "In God, will I praise his word; in the Lord will I praise his saying.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I have hoped in God; I will not be afraid of what man shall do to me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The vows of your praise, O God, which I will pay, are upon me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you have delivered my soul from death, and my feet from sliding, that I should be well-pleasing before God in the land of the living.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 103,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, holy things.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 55,
          "verse": 0
        }
      }
    ]
